  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry, tranquil and increasingly milder into the \nweekend \n\nHigh pressure will control things into Saturday. Low pressure \nwill form over the Bahamas late this week and roll north along \nthe East Coast. There are differences to how each model and \nmembers of the major EFSs track this system. But, they all agree\nwe will be in the squeeze between that storm and the cold front\napproaching from the west at the very same time. The front loses\nalmost all of it's moisture and the trough aloft may arrive\nquickly enough to push that coastal low and it's precip off to\nthe east of PA. But, enough uncertainty exists to keep \nmentioning PoPs and perhaps nudge them up 10% for Sun-Sun PM. \n\nA new high pressure dome then floats overhead for another 2-3 \ndays. Meanwhile...another low may form over the Deep South or \nalong the eastern shore. That feature has a chance to make\nprecip for the CWA sometime between Wed (Day8) and Fri (Day10).\nOf course, Day 9 is Thanksgiving. Temp profiles may generate \nnon-liquid precip. So, we'll need to monitor the evolution of \nthis potential system very carefully. \n\nOf course, this dry stretch with plenty of sun is crisping up \nthe fuels for wildfires. RHs dip into the 20s in southern areas\ntoday and almost everywhere Thursday. Thankfully, the wind is \nlight through the rest of the week.",
